# The figure style of "Deep Learning: Making It Learnable" (press W2 phase 2, F5).
#
# Loaded once per page by one exact line in an existing cell (ruling D6):
#   plt.style.use("../../code/dlbook/book.mplstyle")  # the book's figure style
# (chapters/epilogue.qmd: "../code/dlbook/book.mplstyle"). The notebook manifest ships
# this file as an asset of every unit whose source holds the line.
#
# Sizes are true sizes (ruling D1): data figures are authored at print width, 4.6 in
# (117 mm) or 3.07 in (78 mm), and print at 1:1 in a 120 mm text block. Text: DejaVu
# Sans, 9 pt labels and titles (suptitle, supxlabel and supylabel included), 8 pt ticks
# and legends (ruling D3). Strokes: 1.0 pt for data, 1.6 pt for an emphasized series,
# 0.6 pt for reference lines and guides (D1); the emphasis and reference weights are set
# per artist in the figure code.
#
# The two palettes (ruling D2). Neither is cycled beyond the inks below.
#   Inks, the default for categorical (non-role) series: 1A1A1A, 4D4D4D, 7A7A7A,
#     949494, each series with its own linestyle (-, --, :, -.) or marker (o, s, ^, D),
#     so every series survives grayscale. No two series in one axes share both
#     linestyle and width.
#   Teal 0EA1A1 and magenta 9A0669, a colour-blind-safe pair that may replace two inks
#     where three or more series overlap; linestyles still carry every series. Teal
#     only on strokes of 1.0 pt or heavier, never on text, never dotted.
#   Role colours (tex/macros.tex: 2B6CB0 feature, C05621 parameter, 805AD5 target,
#     2F855A prediction, 722F37 residual) mark roles only and are never cycled.
#   Label text only in 1A1A1A or 4D4D4D: 7A7A7A (4.3:1) and 949494 (3.0:1) are too
#     light for text on white and serve strokes and fills only.
# The cycle below takes the inks in the order 1A1A1A, 7A7A7A, 4D4D4D, 949494, not in
# order of lightness, so adjacent series get more contrast: the first two series of an
# axes differ by the widest step. grid.linewidth is 0.6, the D1 weight of a guide.
#
# Never set here (scripts/audit_figure_style.py rejects them):
#   figure.figsize, figure.dpi, savefig.dpi, savefig.format, savefig.bbox, backend:
#     Quarto's kernel setup and the inline backend own them (fig-format, fig-dpi).
#   figure.constrained_layout.use, figure.autolayout: most cells call tight_layout.
#   axes.spines.*: dropping the top and right spines here would leave an L-shaped half
#     frame on every image axes; the data pass removes them per line axes instead.
#   text.usetex: no LaTeX on the notebook runners.
#   a linestyle or marker in axes.prop_cycle: it would silently dash the second line
#     of every axes that sets no linestyle.
#   any font family or weight matplotlib does not bundle (weights: normal, bold).

## Type: bundled with matplotlib (the same glyphs on the Mac, the Linux runners, Colab)
font.family:           sans-serif
font.sans-serif:       DejaVu Sans
mathtext.fontset:      dejavusans
font.size:             9
axes.titlesize:        9
axes.labelsize:        9
figure.titlesize:      9
figure.labelsize:      9
xtick.labelsize:       8
ytick.labelsize:       8
legend.fontsize:       8
legend.title_fontsize: 8

## Text colour: titles and legend text inherit text.color
text.color:            1A1A1A
axes.labelcolor:       1A1A1A
xtick.labelcolor:      1A1A1A
ytick.labelcolor:      1A1A1A

## Strokes in true points (print floor 0.3 pt)
lines.linewidth:       1.0
lines.markersize:      4
axes.linewidth:        0.8
xtick.major.width:     0.8
ytick.major.width:     0.8
xtick.major.size:      3
ytick.major.size:      3
grid.linewidth:        0.6
grid.color:            D9D9D9

## Furniture
legend.frameon:        False
legend.handlelength:   2.8

## Inks for categorical series: colour only (the linestyle is set per series)
axes.prop_cycle:       cycler('color', ['1A1A1A', '7A7A7A', '4D4D4D', '949494'])

## Output: paths in SVG, TrueType in PDF, stable SVG ids (dates follow SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH)
savefig.pad_inches:    0.04
svg.fonttype:          path
svg.hashsalt:          dl-book
pdf.fonttype:          42
